load ../view-derivation.maude

--- Coverage: a view TRACKS its set. Grown twice from 1, the view's current
--- value is 3.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-VIEW-DERIVATION :
  init =>* qset(s(s(s(z)))) current(v1, s(s(s(z)))) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Coverage: a closed rule does NOT track. It committed at 1, the set has
--- since reached 3, and the rule still reads 1. This is the ruling in one
--- state -- the value a `record` wrote is the value it wrote.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-VIEW-DERIVATION :
  init =>* ruleClosed(r1) qset(s(s(s(z)))) current(r1, s(z)) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Coverage [supersede]: TWO log entries for one view firing, in stamp order,
--- coexisting with ONE current value -- the later one. The log appends, the
--- fact is replaced.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-VIEW-DERIVATION :
  init =>* recordedAt(v1, s(z), M:Cnt) recordedAt(v1, s(s(z)), N:Cnt)
           current(v1, s(s(z))) RESIDUAL:Cfg
  such that lt(M:Cnt, N:Cnt) .

--- Coverage [identity keying]: two view firings over the SAME set hold
--- DIVERGENT current values -- one has re-derived and the other has not.
--- Reachable only because a current cell is keyed by firing, not by class.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-VIEW-DERIVATION :
  init2 =>* current(v1, s(z)) current(v2, s(s(z))) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Coverage: both semantics in one instance at one moment -- the rule frozen
--- at what it saw, the view current with the set.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-VIEW-DERIVATION :
  init =>* ruleClosed(r1) current(r1, s(z)) current(v1, s(s(s(z)))) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Invariant [one-shot]: a rule firing never logs two DIFFERENT values. This
--- is the property the current implementation violates; the bite below
--- reaches exactly this state under today's semantics.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-VIEW-DERIVATION :
  init =>* recordedAt(r1, V:Cnt, M:Cnt) recordedAt(r1, W:Cnt, N:Cnt) RESIDUAL:Cfg
  such that V:Cnt =/= W:Cnt .

--- Invariant [supersede, strong form]: a view firing never holds two current
--- cells AT ALL, equal ones included. One firing, one current value.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-VIEW-DERIVATION :
  init =>* current(v1, V:Cnt) current(v1, V:Cnt) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Invariant [supersede, divergent form]: and never two DIFFERENT ones, which
--- is the accumulation the current implementation exhibits.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-VIEW-DERIVATION :
  init =>* current(v1, V:Cnt) current(v1, W:Cnt) RESIDUAL:Cfg
  such that V:Cnt =/= W:Cnt .

--- Invariant: a closed rule never reopens. Closure is what a settled-firing
--- skip relies on, so it must be terminal.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-VIEW-DERIVATION :
  init =>* ruleClosed(r1) ruleOpen(r1) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Bite: under TODAY's semantics one firing logs two different values -- a
--- plain rule behaving as a live view. Unreachable above, reachable here, so
--- the one-shot invariant is not vacuous.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-LIVE-RULE :
  initLive =>* recordedAt(r1, V:Cnt, M:Cnt) recordedAt(r1, W:Cnt, N:Cnt) RESIDUAL:Cfg
  such that V:Cnt =/= W:Cnt .

--- Bite: and its derived facts ACCUMULATE -- two current values for one
--- firing, the unbounded fact base the ruling removes. This is the state
--- observed live: one firing of `count_them` leaving both {total:1} and
--- {total:2} in the fact base.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-LIVE-RULE :
  initLive =>* current(r1, V:Cnt) current(r1, W:Cnt) RESIDUAL:Cfg
  such that V:Cnt =/= W:Cnt .

--- Refusal [why a view may not create effects]: the view's current value has
--- reached 3 while the effect it enqueued still carries 1. Reachable, and it
--- is what the compile-time refusal exists to prevent.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-VIEW-WITH-EFFECT :
  initEff =>* current(v1, s(s(s(z)))) effInput(v1, s(z)) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Refusal [and the effect can never catch up]: two captured inputs for one
--- effect are unreachable, because the effect id does not depend on the input
--- and the re-lowered effect dedupes. The staleness above is permanent.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-VIEW-WITH-EFFECT :
  initEff =>* effInput(v1, V:Cnt) effInput(v1, W:Cnt) RESIDUAL:Cfg
  such that V:Cnt =/= W:Cnt .

